<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Wednesday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p> B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p> C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p> E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p> F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p> G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p> H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>   Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*  *G*   *H*</p>
<p>Jan 08  21,179 4,094 25,273 13,985 14,078 5,157  0  20,092</p>
<p>Jan 09  21,199 4,280 25,479 13,942 14,014 5,396  0  20,125</p>
<p>Jan 10  21,211 4,451 25,662 13,920 13,970 5,490  0  20,028</p>
<p>Jan 13  21,066 4,449 25,515 13,901 13,966 5,426  0  19,865</p>
<p>Jan 14  20,980 4,377 25,357 13,757 13,812 5,537  0  19,776</p>
<p>Jan 15  20,896 4,439 25,335 13,667 13,724 5,643  0  19,680</p>
<p>Jan 16  20,758 4,591 25,349 13,650 13,703 5,537  0  19,550</p>
<p>Jan 17  20,470 4,457 24,927 13,606 13,651 5,293  0  19,203</p>
<p>Jan 20  20,477 4,457 24,934 13,597 13,607 5,338  0  19,204</p>
<p>*A  Of the $20.48 billion in international reserves, $2.41 billion (11.78 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0651))</p>
</text>
